[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. The reports merged into it
hold three problems, and the queued parser fix closes only one of them. Each problem now has a
ticket of its own.

<Callout kind="warn">
Fixing the parser leaves two problems open: the booking-v3 form hint, and invites that move by a
day across time zones. Do not close #4471's reports as fixed until all three tickets are closed.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

## How to tell them apart

- **`parser`**: day and month swapped ("Booked for 2 March. The invite says 3 February."). A day-first tenant,
  any channel except a booking-v3 form. The shared parser reads month first.
- **`hint`**: the same swap, but only from booking-v3 forms at day-first tenants. The form prints
  `MM/DD/YYYY` as its hint, people type what it says, and the form reads it day first. The swap
  happens in the form, so a parser fix does not reach it.
- **`move`**: no swap at all. The date moves by one day, differs by where the attendee is
  (Lisbon Tuesday, Toronto Monday), or the invite is stamped before the booking. That is a
  time-zone fault. The desk read these by hand (`oneDayMove` in the desk notes) and then filed
  them under `parser` by tenant.

Intake's tag (`parser` / `hint`) is a guess from the reporter's browser, so the table counts by
tenant and channel instead, with `causes.ts`. Repeated rows in the export count once.

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports whose subject lines match.
All three problems arrive with the same subjects ("Wrong day on the invite", "Date is wrong"), so
subject matching put them in one ticket. Merging by subject needs a new decision record: merge by
cause, as `causes.ts` already computes it.

